  "body": "Auction: 34 Shortland Street, City on Wednesday 11 November 2026 at 10:00AM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nWelcome to Light House, a striking 452m² (approx.) Abodo-clad residence designed by Dylan Rhynd of DPRD Studio Architecture, where innovative design, exceptional craftsmanship and contemporary luxury come together.\r\n\r\nThree dramatic full-length skylights and expansive glazing flood the interiors with natural light. Honed and polished concrete, tactile stone and French oak create a sophisticated yet welcoming palette, while an impressive entrance foyer, striking architectural staircase and elevated walkway highlight the home's distinctive character. The thoughtfully configured layout places the main living areas and four of the five bedrooms together on the upper level.\r\n\r\nAt the heart of the home, a spectacular designer kitchen features a distinctive oak and marble island, integrated Fisher & Paykel appliances and a generous scullery. Open-plan family living and a separate lounge flow seamlessly to sheltered Louvretech decks, an outdoor gas fireplace and barbecue area. Beyond, landscaped entertaining spaces surround the heated saltwater swimming pool, while private, fully fenced gardens and a raised AstroTurf terrace provide an idyllic setting for relaxation and recreation.\r\n\r\nFive generous bedrooms are complemented by three elegantly appointed bathrooms and a guest powder room, with the family bathroom providing direct access to an outdoor shower. Underfloor heating, ducted air conditioning and Warm Roof technology ensure year-round comfort, while sophisticated smart-home automation allows remote control of lighting, security, blinds and entertainment. Substantial four-car garaging provides ample space for vehicles and recreational equipment.\r\n\r\nPerfectly positioned close to the Bays beaches, cafés, parks, Madills Farm Reserve and sought-after schools, including Kohimarama School and Glendowie College, Light House combines architectural distinction, privacy and convenience in one remarkable family sanctuary.\r\n\r\nSee interactive features for this property on barfoot.co.nz. Click the \"View office website\" link at the bottom of this page.",
